{"diagnosis": "Loopback send 0xa5 never sets recv_buf_valid so reg_dat_do stays ~0 (line 53) vs expected 0xa5, causing TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received and tohost FAIL 0xdead at 22023 cycles. CONE_SLICE only lists picosoc/spiflash.v:52 bytecount and scripts/quartus/system.v:57 out_byte_en with no simpleuart RX driver, so trace wins. Root cause is line 39 reg [3:1] recv_state missing bit0, so the RX state machine cannot sequence through start/data/stop states.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@
 	reg [31:0] cfg_divider;

-	reg [3:1] recv_state;
+	reg [3:0] recv_state;
 	reg [31:0] recv_divcnt;
 	reg [7:0] recv_pattern;
 	reg [7:0] recv_buf_data;
", "expected": "tohost PASS with byte 0xa5 received, no TRAP: uart timeout"}

